  <h2>Trim and equipment differences</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Momentum:</strong> equipment-focused baseline with available upgrades varying by market and package.</li>
    <li><strong>R-Design:</strong> sport-oriented seats, steering wheel, upholstery and decorative trim on applicable builds.</li>
    <li><strong>Inscription:</strong> comfort- and luxury-oriented seat, material and decorative details.</li>
    <li><strong>Recharge / Polestar Engineered:</strong> hybrid-specific displays or controls and performance-specific trim may be present.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Seat heating, ventilation, power adjustment, memory, rear-seat heating, steering-wheel heating, premium audio, navigation, head-up display and other features are option-dependent. Confirm what is installed in the individual car before following a control walkthrough or ordering a replacement component.</p>
  <div class="note"><strong>Safety:</strong> airbags, seat-belt pretensioners and their wiring are safety-critical. Do not probe SRS connectors or remove restraint components without the correct Volvo service procedure.</div>
